The three main types of affordable housing defined in Annex B: Glossary are: 
a. Social Rent, which meets specific conditions including rent set in accordance with the government's rent policy, landlord being a registered provider, and provisions to remain at an affordable price (Draft_NPPF_December_2025, Annex B); 
b. Other affordable housing for rent, which includes Affordable Private Rent for Build to Rent schemes and has conditions such as rent set in accordance with the government's rent policy or at least 20% below local market rents (Draft_NPPF_December_2025, Annex B); 
c. Discounted market sales housing, which is sold at a discount of at least 20% below local market value and has provisions to remain at a discount for future eligible households (Draft_NPPF_December_2025, Annex B).

Additionally, two more types are mentioned: 
d. Other affordable routes to home ownership, which includes shared ownership, relevant equity loans, and rent to buy (Draft_NPPF_December_2025, Annex B); 
e. Military affordable housing, which meets specific conditions including sub-market military rent and provisions to remain as affordable housing for future eligible households (Draft_NPPF_December_2025, Annex B).

References:
- [Source 1]: Draft_NPPF_December_2025.pdf — Annex B
